// #483/#490 - Circle VIII's 6 summon spells. All previously dead commented-out stub content
// (unimplementedSpells.def, old pre-port SPELLFLAG_* syntax) - header numbers (58, 60-64) carried
// over unchanged from that stub so history/numbering stays traceable. Target NPCDef content
// already exists in summons.def (confirmed real, mage-tier variants - NOT the overpowered wild
// monster chardefs that happen to share a similar name): c_vortex_mage, c_elem_air_m,
// c_elem_earth_m, c_elem_fire_m, c_elem_water_m, c_daemon_mage1. Checked each chardef's own
// NAME=/DEFNAME= pairing for the off-by-one alignment glitch flagged during #483's research -
// none found, every NAME= matches its own DEFNAME= correctly (Vortex/c_vortex_mage, Elemental
// Vzduchu["air" in Czech]/c_elem_air_m, Elemental Zeme["earth"]/c_elem_earth_m, Elemental
// Ohne["fire"]/c_elem_fire_m, Elemental Vody["water"]/c_elem_water_m, Summon/c_daemon_mage1).
//
// All Hostile left at its false default (normal controlled pet, same as Phase 4's Summon
// Creature) - these are classic leashed mage pets, not Blade Spirits-shaped autonomous hostiles.
// SummonSpellDef.On_EffectGround only sets ControlMaster/Flag_WarMode/the summoned-creature tag/
// the despawn timer - it never touches AI/brain/ability fields, so each chardef's own AI comes
// through unmodified: Energy Vortex keeps its more aggressive brain_beserk + roundattack (a
// pet/creature with a periodic AoE melee ability, NOT an AoE damage field despite the spell's
// name), while the 4 elementals keep their plain/docile AI - no extra wiring needed to preserve
// that distinction, it's already a property of the chardef itself.
//
// RUNES/CASTTIME/MANAUSE/Requirements/DURATION all carried over unchanged from the stub -
// explicitly NOT confirmed live-Erebor values (same caveat as every other Circle VIII number),
// GM-tunable via .settings like every other summon this session, kept as placeholders rather than
// hand-guessed. RUNEITEM/SCROLLITEM point at real pre-existing converted content (itemb7.def/
// scrolls.def) - confirmed present, not newly authored. SOUND left at 0, same reasoning as every
// other summon spell this phase/session - none of the old snd_SPELL_* tokens resolve to anything
// real (confirmed: no .def/.cs file defines any of them).
//
// Optional Erebor mechanic (staff-tier gating: teak for the elementals/vortex, mahogany for
// Daemon) explicitly DEFERRED here, same treatment as every other optional per-weapon-tier gate
// this session (overlaps the known #157/#393 weapon-staff-tier-data-quality gaps) - not built.

[SummonSpellDef 58]
DEFNAME=s_energy_vortex
NAME=Energy Vortex
SOUND=0
RUNES=VCP
CASTTIME=4.0
RUNEITEM=i_rune_energy_vortex
SCROLLITEM=i_scroll_energy_vortex
FLAGS=SpellFlag.CanTargetAnything | SpellFlag.CanEffectGround | SpellFlag.EffectNeedsLOS
EFFECT=0
DURATION=1*60.0,3*60.0
MANAUSE=50
Requirements=80.0 Magery
summonChar=c_vortex_mage

on=@effectGround
	EffectFactory.StationaryEffectAt(this, 0x3728, 10, 20)

[SummonSpellDef 60]
DEFNAME=s_summon_elem_air
NAME=Air Elemental
SOUND=0
RUNES=KVXH
CASTTIME=4.0
RUNEITEM=i_rune_summon_elem_air
